cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QuantumLab in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "QuantumLab: Quantum Simulation Framework"
abstract: >-
  A Python framework for numerical quantum mechanics. It solves the
  time-dependent Schrödinger and Gross–Pitaevskii equations in 1D, 2D and 3D
  with split-step Fourier methods of order 2 and 4, including time-dependent
  potentials, rotating frames, imaginary-time and matrix-free eigensolvers,
  optional CUDA GPU acceleration, and 3D isosurface rendering. Results are
  validated against analytic and independent numerical references.
